content.text:
Half of it was. Trimmed 8 lines to 3 in `e36be30`, pushed to #554.

The first paragraph restated the definition it sat above — `dockerfile` discriminating the sources *is* the disjunction on the next line, `target`/`testConfig` being android-only *is* the `if` block, and the Windows exclusions were already explained inline on the two fields they pin. That made it the only 8-line comment in an 87-line file with 8 comment lines total.

The second paragraph stays: that a bare `#LinuxImage | #WindowsImage` disjunction fails because CUE reports every field of both branches as incomplete is a dead end a reader would otherwise rediscover by trying it.

```cue
// One published image. Conditional fields rather than a disjunction
// (#LinuxImage | #WindowsImage): CUE cannot pick a branch and reports every
// field of both as incomplete.
```

Re-ran `cue vet` on both manifests and the five adversarial cases (Windows `scout: true` / `prTag: true`, missing `testConfig`, unknown field, empty array) — all still rejected, so the constraints are untouched.

